sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant O as Owner
    participant N as Nodes on the path
    participant R as Replicas (k closest to the DID)
    Note over O: record at any position = algorithm | signature | DID Document<br/>key = the SHA-256 of the genesis, the DID's suffix
    O->>N: FIND_NODE(key), iterative, alpha at a time
    N-->>O: closer nodes
    Note over O: no copy is read first, the k closest are the replicas
    par to each replica
        O->>R: STORE(key, record)
        Note over R: decides by what it holds, or checks the network<br/>(see the replica rules and the STORE check)
        R-->>O: Stored, AlreadyStored, or a refusal
    end
    opt a replica refused (Conflict, Stale)
        O->>R: FIND_VALUE(key) to each replica that refused, at once
        R-->>O: its record, or nothing
        Note over O: would a holder of it refuse? then its signature<br/>another record at the same position: ExistingRecord<br/>a higher position: NewerVersion<br/>anything else: a replica that did not store
    end
    Note over O: Complete if every replica stored it,<br/>Degraded if some did not, or refused without showing why
